  "enhanced_information": "Endochondral ossification occurs in long bones, not flat bones like those in the skull. The ossification of long bones begins in the diaphysis, not the epiphyses. The articular cartilage does not constitute the growth plate or epiphyseal plate. Resorption tunnels allow for bone remodeling by osteoclasts, not perforating cones. The structure of articular cartilage is part of the epiphyseal cartilage."
